>
  <!-- 1. Introduction -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="introduction" class="guide-h2">What this guide covers</h2>
    <p>
      This is a practical companion for getting{" "}
      <a href="/tools/claude-code/">Claude Code</a> installed, authenticated, and
      verified — without drowning in ecosystem theory. It is for{" "}
      <strong>new users</strong> who want a clean first setup, and for anyone
      reinstalling after a machine change or a broken PATH.
    </p>
    <p>
      You will get: requirements, the recommended install path (plus solid
      alternatives), first-time auth, a minimal day-one config, troubleshooting,
      then links into the rest of the Claude Code hub (skills, plugins, MCP,
      pricing, comparisons).
    </p>
    <InfoCallout title="Data updated: August 2026" variant="info">
      <p>
        Installer URLs, package managers, and plan packaging change. Prefer{" "}
        <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup">official Claude Code setup
        docs</a>{" "}
        if a command below fails.{" "}
        <strong
          >Claude Code needs a paid Claude plan (Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise) or
          Console/API access — Free chat alone is not enough.</strong
        >
      </p>
    </InfoCallout>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Key takeaway -->
  <section id="key-takeaway">
    <h2 class="guide-h2">Key takeaway</h2>
    <KeyTakeaway>
      Fastest reliable path: use the{" "}
      <strong>native installer</strong> (
      <code>curl … | bash</code> on macOS/Linux/WSL, PowerShell script on
      Windows) → run <code>claude</code> → complete browser login on a Pro+ (or
      API) account → open a real project → ask for a small safe change → run{" "}
      <code>claude doctor</code> if anything fails. Skip npm, plugins, and MCP
      until that loop works.
    </KeyTakeaway>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Requirements -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="requirements" class="guide-h2">System requirements</h2>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Supported platforms (typical 2026 docs)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>macOS</strong> 13.0+
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Windows</strong> 10 (1809+) or Windows Server 2019+ (native
        PowerShell/CMD; WSL also common for dev workflows)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Linux</strong> — Ubuntu 20.04+, Debian 10+, Alpine 3.19+, and
        similar modern distros
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hardware</strong> — roughly 4 GB+ RAM; x64 or ARM64
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Network</strong> — outbound internet for install, auth, and model
        calls
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Prerequisites</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A <strong>Claude account with Code access</strong> — Pro, Max, Team, or
        Enterprise (or Anthropic Console / approved API path). See{" "}
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/pricing/">Claude Code pricing</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        A terminal you actually use (Terminal.app, iTerm, Windows Terminal, etc.)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Git</strong> installed if you expect normal repo workflows
        (especially on Windows Desktop Code tab)
      </li>
      <li>
        For the <strong>npm install path only</strong>: Node.js 22+ (native
        installer does <em>not</em> require Node)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Commonly missed</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Being on Claude Free and wondering why Code never unlocks
      </li>
      <li>
        Installing via npm with <code>sudo</code> (permission mess — do not)
      </li>
      <li>
        Two installs at once (old npm global + new native) fighting on PATH
      </li>
      <li>
        Corporate proxy / firewall blocking auth or API hosts
      </li>
      <li>
        Expecting Desktop “Code” without a paid plan that includes Code
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Installation methods -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="install" class="guide-h2">Installation methods</h2>

    <h3 class="guide-h3">1. Official native installer (recommended)</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>When to use:</strong> Almost always — first install on a personal
      machine. No Node required; ships the native binary and update path Anthropic
      documents first.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Steps — macOS, Linux, WSL:</strong></p>
    <pre
      class="not-prose my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-border bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-ink"
    ><code>curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
    <p><strong>Steps — Windows PowerShell:</strong></p>
    <pre
      class="not-prose my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-border bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-ink"
    ><code>irm https://claude.ai/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>
    <p>
      <strong>Windows CMD:</strong> official docs also provide an{" "}
      <code>install.cmd</code> download-and-run flow if you are not on PowerShell.
    </p>
    <p>
      After install, open a <strong>new</strong> terminal and verify:
    </p>
    <pre
      class="not-prose my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-border bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-ink"
    ><code>claude --version
claude doctor</code></pre>
    <InfoCallout title="Common failure points" variant="warning">
      <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>
          Shell still using an old session — restart the terminal after install
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>claude: command not found</code> — PATH not updated; re-source
          shell config or reinstall
        </li>
        <li>
          Policy blocks on corporate Windows — need admin/IT approval for scripts
        </li>
        <li>
          Curl/TLS failures — proxy or outdated CA store
        </li>
      </ul>
    </InfoCallout>

    <h3 class="guide-h3">2. Package managers (Homebrew / WinGet)</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>When to use:</strong> You already manage tools via brew or winget
      and want upgrades in that workflow.
    </p>
    <pre
      class="not-prose my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-border bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-ink"
    ><code># macOS (Homebrew cask — confirm formula name if brew search differs)
brew install --cask claude-code

# Windows
winget install Anthropic.ClaudeCode</code></pre>
    <p>
      <strong>Failure points:</strong> stale cask mirrors, wrong package ID,
      brew/winget not on PATH, needing a full logout after first install.
    </p>

    <h3 class="guide-h3">3. npm global (alternative CLI path)</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>When to use:</strong> Node 22+ is already standard in your
      environment, or you pin versions via npm. Official docs still support this;
      native installer remains the default recommendation for new users.
    </p>
    <pre
      class="not-prose my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-border bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-ink"
    ><code>npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
claude --version</code></pre>
    <p>
      The package typically installs the same native binary style under the hood.
      <strong>Do not use <code>sudo npm install -g</code></strong> — fix npm
      permissions or use a version manager instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Failure points:</strong> Node too old (EBADENGINE warnings), global
      bin directory not on PATH, conflict with a separate native install (uninstall
      one: <code>npm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code</code>).
    </p>

    <h3 class="guide-h3">4. Claude Desktop (Code tab)</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>When to use:</strong> You want a GUI session model (Code tab inside
      Claude Desktop) rather than living only in the terminal. Still requires a
      plan that includes Claude Code.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Download Claude Desktop from Anthropic’s download page for macOS, Windows,
        or Linux (beta where offered).
      </li>
      <li>Install, launch, and sign in with your Claude account.</li>
      <li>
        Open the <strong>Code</strong> tab. On Windows, install Git for Windows if
        prompted and restart the app.
      </li>
      <li>
        Point a session at a project folder and run a small task to verify.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <strong>Failure points:</strong> Free plan without Code; missing Git on
      Windows; corporate device management blocking the app; confusing Desktop Chat
      with the Code product surface.
    </p>
    <InfoCallout title="CLI vs Desktop" variant="tip">
      <p>
        Most of this hub assumes the <strong>CLI agent</strong> workflow. Desktop
        Code is valid for GUI-first users; advanced skills/plugins/MCP workflows
        are still easiest to document and automate from the terminal CLI.
      </p>
    </InfoCallout>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. First-time setup -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="first-time" class="guide-h2">First-time setup</h2>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Authentication</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>
        In a terminal, <code>cd</code> to a project you care about (or an empty
        test folder with a git repo).
      </li>
      <li>
        Run <code>claude</code> (or the documented login command if your build
        separates it).
      </li>
      <li>
        Complete the <strong>browser login</strong> when prompted. Use the same
        account that has Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise (or Console).
      </li>
      <li>
        If you use API keys instead: set{" "}
        <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> per official auth docs; Claude Code may
        prompt once to approve the key rather than opening a browser.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Team/Enterprise users may need org SSO and admin-enabled Code access — if
      login succeeds but Code is denied, check plan and org settings, not the
      installer.
    </p>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Initial configuration</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Accept sensible permission defaults for the first session; tighten later.
      </li>
      <li>
        Prefer working inside a real git repository so diffs and reverts stay easy.
      </li>
      <li>
        Optional: add a short project <code>CLAUDE.md</code> with stack, test
        command, and “do not touch” paths — keep it small on day one.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Recommended starting settings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>One project at a time — do not enable every MCP globally yet</li>
      <li>
        Explicit approvals for shell commands until you trust the workflow
      </li>
      <li>
        Use a branch for the first agent edits
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Verify everything works</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <code>claude --version</code> prints a version
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>claude doctor</code> reports no critical failures
      </li>
      <li>
        Inside a repo: ask Claude to explain the project structure (read-only)
      </li>
      <li>
        Ask for a trivial change (comment or README line), review the diff, accept
        or reject
      </li>
      <li>
        Run your usual tests/lint if the change warrants it
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      If step 1–2 fail, fix install/PATH/auth before adding skills or plugins.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Recommended first config -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="first-config" class="guide-h2">
      Recommended first configuration
    </h2>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Useful defaults (day one)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Native CLI install + browser auth on a paid plan
      </li>
      <li>
        Project opened from its git root
      </li>
      <li>
        Short <code>CLAUDE.md</code>: language, package manager, test command,
        code style links
      </li>
      <li>
        No marketplace megapacks yet
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Add later (with links)</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/skills/">Skills</a> — when you repeat the
        same checklist or release process
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/plugins/">Plugins</a> — when you want a
        maintained bundle (e.g. GitHub integration) via marketplace
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/mcp/">MCP servers</a> — GitHub, Context7,
        Playwright first; only what you use weekly
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">What not to over-configure on day one</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Twenty MCP servers and three community plugin marketplaces</li>
      <li>
        Aggressive always-on hooks you have not read
      </li>
      <li>
        Production DB credentials “just to try”
      </li>
      <li>
        Dual native + npm installs “for safety”
      </li>
      <li>
        Max 20x spend before you know your usage pattern — start on the plan you
        have; upgrade when limits block real work (
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/pricing/">pricing</a>)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <KeyTakeaway>
      Day-one success = <strong>install + auth + one real edit in a real
      repo</strong>. Ecosystem depth comes after that baseline is boringly
      reliable.
    </KeyTakeaway>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. Troubleshooting -->
  <section>
    <h2 id="troubleshooting" class="guide-h2">
      Common setup problems &amp; fixes
    </h2>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Installation errors</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Script fails mid-download</strong> — retry; check network/proxy;
        try package manager path
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>npm EBADENGINE / weird globals</strong> — upgrade Node to 22+, or
        switch to native installer
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Permission denied on global npm</strong> — never sudo; fix npm
        prefix or use nvm/fnm
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Permission issues</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Claude cannot write files — check directory ownership and sandbox/approval
        prompts
      </li>
      <li>
        macOS privacy prompts for terminal disk access — allow for your terminal
        app
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Auth problems</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Browser never opens / callback fails — complete login URL manually if
        shown; check popup blockers
      </li>
      <li>
        Logged in but no Code — plan is Free or org has not enabled Code
      </li>
      <li>
        API key rejected — wrong env var, expired key, or key without required
        access
      </li>
      <li>
        SSO loops on Team/Enterprise — finish org login in browser; contact admin
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Path / environment issues</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>command not found: claude</code> — new terminal; verify install
        location on PATH; remove duplicate installs
      </li>
      <li>
        Wrong binary version — <code>which claude</code> /{" "}
        <code>Get-Command claude</code>; uninstall the stale one
      </li>
      <li>
        WSL vs Windows native confusion — install and run in the environment where
        your code lives
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide-h3">Quick troubleshooting checklist</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>New terminal window</li>
      <li>
        <code>claude --version</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>claude doctor</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        Confirm paid plan / org access
      </li>
      <li>
        Only one install method active
      </li>
      <li>
        Network can reach Anthropic auth/API endpoints
      </li>
      <li>
        Retry login; only then reinstall
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Deeper symptom → fix coverage (performance, skills, plugins, MCP, model
      issues):{" "}
      <a href="/guides/claude-code/troubleshooting/"
        >Claude Code troubleshooting guide</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

